Could he potentially change

00:08:18.965 --> 00:08:19.665
that perception?

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:20.600
How much does that matter

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.668
going into this early primary stage?

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:23.369
I've observed

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:24.971
a lot of presidential candidates

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:25.671
on the campaign trail

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:26.973
get better at retail politics,

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:27.740
even if they don't

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:29.575
have an initial sort of

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:30.776
affinity for that.

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:31.210
In fact,

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:31.944
some of the reports

00:08:31.944 --> 00:08:33.279
from his second New Hampshire

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:35.281
trip was a market improvement

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:36.616
from the first New Hampshire

00:08:36.616 --> 00:08:38.484
trip on this. So we'll see.

00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:39.552
This is part of,

00:08:39.552 --> 00:08:40.887
you know, members of Congress

00:08:40.887 --> 00:08:42.388
he served with when he was in the House

00:08:42.388 --> 00:08:43.623
did not think of him as somebody

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:46.158
that was all that collegial or friendly

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:46.792
or you know,

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:48.861
so he this is definitely something

00:08:48.861 --> 00:08:50.897
that I think observers and voters

00:08:50.897 --> 00:08:53.099
will be watching on the campaign trail.

00:08:53.299 --> 00:08:54.133
But I don't believe that's

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:56.469
the kind of thing that can't be improved.

00:08:56.469 --> 00:08:57.103
I remember

00:08:58.104 --> 00:08:58.404
a guy

00:08:58.404 --> 00:08:59.238
named Barack Obama

00:08:59.238 --> 00:09:00.840
who wasn't like all the greatest

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.375
in retail politics initially,

00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:03.776
but he learned and got better

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:05.077
throughout his time on the trail.

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:06.145
He really did.

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:07.179
He really did.

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:08.714
David Chalian, thank you so much.

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:09.715
And to Jessica Dean

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:11.317
as well for her quick reporting.

00:09:11.317 --> 00:09:11.951
Thank you so much.

